{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user asked me to build the cinema seat-booking web application described in `spec/README.md`, implemented as the existing Angular application in the Nx workspace (Nx project `cinescope` in `apps/cinescope`). The technology stack is described in `spec/stack.md`. The work is explicitly split into ordered tickets in `spec/tickets/` (01 through 07) that must be implemented **in order**. The user stated `spec/README.md` is \"the complete specification: do not ask any questions, and where it is silent choose the simplest option that satisfies it.\" The task is only finished when **every ticket is done** and `pnpm nx build cinescope` succeeds. No other explicit user messages were given during the session (the only chat-level instruction was this initial task description, plus the final system-level instruction forcing this plain-text summary with no tool calls).\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Nx 23 monorepo; Angular 22 standalone, **zoneless** change detection (no Zone.js — relies on Angular Signals for reactivity); Angular Router with `withComponentInputBinding()` so route params bind directly to component `input()` signals; Angular Material 22 + CDK (Material theme applied via `@use '@angular/material' as mat;` in styles.scss); native date adapter (`provideNativeDateAdapter()`) for the Material datepicker; SCSS; Vitest for unit tests; ESLint; pnpm as the only allowed package manager (never npm/yarn); **no new dependencies allowed** (`@angular/animations` is NOT installed — `provideAnimationsAsync()` must not be used).\n   - Backend: `json-server` 0.17.4 serving `db.json` from workspace root at `http://localhost:3000`, started via `pnpm api`; CORS enabled; data model `Movie`, `Screening` (with `occupiedSeats: string[]`), `Reservation`; seat identifiers `R<row>C<column>`; couches occupy two identifiers.\n   - `sessionStorage`-backed booking state machine (section 3.1 of spec): a booking holds screening id, selected seats, checkout form values, paid flag, and (once paid) customer email; route-entry guards enforce access rules (seat map: screening must exist; summary/checkout: unpaid booking matching screening id with ≥1 seat; confirmation: paid booking) — checks run **only on route entry**, not continuously.\n   - Toasts: exactly one visible at a time, auto-dismiss after 4000ms — implemented via Angular Material's `MatSnackBar` (which already enforces \"one at a time\" semantics) hosting a custom `ToastComponent` via `openFromComponent`.\n   - Auditorium geometry: 15 rows × 24 columns, two 2-seat-wide aisles (between columns 4/5 and 20/21), entrance gap replacing columns 1–4 in rows 1–10, accessible seats at row 1 columns 10–15, couches (paired columns) filling all of row 15 (12 couches), implemented via a CSS Grid with 28 tracks (via a `columnTrack()` mapping function) rather than iterating raw column indices, to cleanly handle gaps/aisles/label columns.\n   - Pricing tiers: rows 1–5 → 25.00 PLN, 6–10 → 32.00 PLN, 11–14 → 39.00 PLN, couches (row 15) → 89.00 PLN flat per couch; prices always formatted with two decimals + \" PLN\" suffix.\n   - Custom checkout validation (NOT using Angular Reactive Forms — implemented as plain pure functions + signals) per spec's exact wording: required vs. rule-specific error messages, \"touched\"/\"submitted\" gating of message visibility, re-evaluation of confirm-email when email changes, phone optional-but-strict-9-digits, custom email-validity algorithm (single `@`, non-empty local/domain without spaces/`@`, domain must contain a `.` with ≥1 character on each side).\n   - `data-testid` contract (section 9 of spec) is exhaustive and exact — must not rename/abbreviate/prefix, and must not reuse testids elsewhere; many elements also carry specific data attributes (`data-row`, `data-column`, `data-state`, `data-selected`, etc.) with exact value formats (plain numbers vs. ISO dates vs. `\"true\"/\"false\"` strings).\n   - Headless browser smoke-testing approach: `playwright-core` (not `playwright`) installed in a scratch directory outside the project, driving the pre-cached Chromium binary at `/opt/ms-playwright/chromium-1234/chrome-linux/chrome` with `--no-sandbox`, to visually/functionally verify the implementation against the spec by reading `data-testid` attributes/text and taking screenshots.\n   - Important environment nuance: the real \"today\" date in this sandbox is **2026-10-15**, while all `db.json` screenings are dated 2026-09-15 through 2026-09-21 (entirely in the past relative to \"today\") — per spec section 2.2 this is expected and must NOT be worked around by changing `db.json` or the date logic; the movie list will correctly show \"No screenings on this day\" for every day in its 5-day window, so testing screens downstream of the movie list must navigate directly by URL (e.g., `/screenings/1/seats`) rather than by clicking through from `/`.\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n\n   - **`spec/README.md`, `spec/stack.md`, `spec/tickets/*.md`** (read-only): Full specification consumed in detail; ticket order is 01-movie-list → 02-auditorium-map → 03-seat-selection → 04-booking-summary → 05-checkout → 06-confirmation → 07-final-pass (each blocked by the previous).\n\n   - **`apps/cinescope/src/app/core/models.ts`** (created): Defines `Movie`, `Screening`, `ReservationCustomer`, `Reservation`, `CheckoutFormValues`, `Booking`, `ScreeningData` interfaces matching spec's TypeScript data model in section 2.1, plus the app's own `Booking`/`CheckoutFormValues`/`ScreeningData` types for internal state.\n\n   - **`apps/cinescope/src/app/core/api.service.ts`** (created, then fixed): `ApiService` (`providedIn: 'root'`) wrapping `HttpClient` calls to `http://localhost:3000` — `getMovies`, `getMovie(id)`, `getScreenings`, `getScreening(id)`, `getMovieAndScreening(screeningId)` (switchMap screening→movie), `getMoviesAndScreenings()` (forkJoin), `createReservation(payload)` (POST `/reservations`). Fixed: removed an unused `HttpParams` import that would have caused a lint/unused-import issue.\n\n   - **`apps/cinescope/src/app/core/date.util.ts`** (created): `startOfDay`, `addDays`, `toIsoDate`, `isValidIsoDate` (regex `^\\d{4}-\\d{2}-\\d{2}$` plus round-trip validity check against `Date.parse`), `parseIsoDate`, `weekdayFull` (via `toLocaleDateString('en-US', {weekday:'long'})`), `monthShort` (via `{month:'short'}`), `formatShowDate(isoDate, time)` producing e.g. `\"Tuesday 15 Sep 16:00\"`.\n\n   - **`apps/cinescope/src/app/core/seat.util.ts`** (created): `parseSeatId`/`seatId` (regex `^R(\\d+)C(\\d+)$`), `sortSeatIds` (sort by row then column), `COUCH_ROW=15`, `COUCH_PRICE=89`, `priceForRow(row)` (25/32/39 tiers for rows ≤5/≤10/else), `formatPrice`, `BookingItem` interface (`type: 'seat'|'couch'`, row, column or columnStart/columnEnd, price, seatIds), `buildBookingItems(ids)` (groups raw seat ids into ordered seat/couch items — couches paired by `column % 2 === 1 ? column : column-1`), `groupItemsByRow`, `panelSeatLabel` (e.g. `\"1-2\"`), `summarySeatLabel` (e.g. `\"Couch 1-2\"`).\n\n   - **`apps/cinescope/src/app/core/auditorium.util.ts`** (created): Grid-track-based layout engine. Key exports: `TOTAL_ROWS=15`, `TOTAL_COLUMNS=24`, `LEFT_LABEL_TRACK=1`, `AISLE_TRACK_1=6`, `AISLE_TRACK_2=23`, `RIGHT_LABEL_TRACK=28`, `columnTrack(column)` (maps global column 1–24 to a CSS grid track, skipping aisle/label tracks: `col<=4 → col+1`, `col<=20 → col+2`, `else → col+3`), `SeatCell`/`CouchCell`/`AisleCell`/`EmptyCell`/`RowCell` types, `ROW_LAYOUTS: RowLayout[]` precomputed for all 15 rows via `buildBlock(row, colStart, colEnd)` (handles couches-only row 15, entrance-empty rows 1–10 columns 1–4, else individual seats with `isAccessible(row,col)` = row===1 && col in [10,15]) and `buildRow(row)` (assembles block1 + aisle1 + block2 + aisle2 + block3).\n\n   - **`apps/cinescope/src/app/core/booking.service.ts`** (created): `BookingService` (`providedIn: 'root'`), `STORAGE_KEY='cinescope.booking'`, signal-backed state persisted via `effect()` to `sessionStorage`. Key methods: `ensureBookingForScreening(screeningId)` (resets to empty booking unless current one matches screeningId and is unpaid), `hasUnpaidSeatsFor(screeningId)`, `hasPaidBooking()`, `toggleSeats(ids): 'added'|'removed'|'limit-exceeded'` (atomic pair toggling for couches; max 10 total seat ids), `removeSeats(ids)`, `updateForm(patch)`, `markPaid(email)`, `clear()`. Example snippet:\n     ```ts\n     toggleSeats(ids: string[]): ToggleResult {\n       const booking = this.bookingSignal();\n       if (!booking) return 'removed';\n       const set = new Set(booking.seats);\n       const allSelected = ids.every((id) => set.has(id));\n       if (allSelected) {\n         ids.forEach((id) => set.delete(id));\n         this.bookingSignal.set({ ...booking, seats: [...set] });\n         return 'removed';\n       }\n       if (set.size + ids.length > MAX_SEATS) return 'limit-exceeded';\n       ids.forEach((id) => set.add(id));\n       this.bookingSignal.set({ ...booking, seats: [...set] });\n       return 'added';\n     }\n     ```\n\n   - **`apps/cinescope/src/app/core/guards.ts`** (created): `bookingGuard` and `confirmationGuard` (`CanActivateFn`), both returning `router.parseUrl('/')` on failure, else `true`.\n\n   - **`apps/cinescope/src/app/shared/toast/toast.component.ts`** (created): Minimal `ToastComponent` reading `MAT_SNACK_BAR_DATA`, template `<span data-testid=\"toast\">{{ data.message }}</span>`.\n\n   - **`apps/cinescope/src/app/core/toast.service.ts`** (created): `ToastService.show(message)` → `MatSnackBar.openFromComponent(ToastComponent, { data: { message }, duration: 4000, horizontalPosition: 'center', verticalPosition: 'bottom' })`.\n\n   - **`apps/cinescope/src/app/core/validation.util.ts`** (created): `isValidEmail(value)` (custom single-`@`, non-space local/domain, domain-must-contain-interior-dot logic) and `isValidPhone(value)` (`/^\\d{9}$/`).\n\n   - **`apps/cinescope/src/app/app.config.ts`** (rewritten twice): Final version:\n     ```ts\n     import { provideHttpClient } from '@angular/common/http';\n     import { ApplicationConfig, provideBrowserGlobalErrorListeners } from '@angular/core';\n     import { provideNativeDateAdapter } from '@angular/material/core';\n     import { provideRouter, withComponentInputBinding } from '@angular/router';\n     import { appRoutes } from './app.routes';\n\n     export const appConfig: ApplicationConfig = {\n       providers: [\n         provideBrowserGlobalErrorListeners(),\n         provideRouter(appRoutes, withComponentInputBinding()),\n         provideNativeDateAdapter(),\n         provideHttpClient(),\n       ],\n     };\n     ```\n     (Initially included `provideAnimationsAsync()` from `@angular/platform-browser/animations/async`, which broke the build because `@angular/animations` isn't an installed dependency — removed.)\n\n   - **`apps/cinescope/src/app/app.routes.ts`** (rewritten): 5 routes — `''` (MovieList, no guard), `screenings/:id/seats` (SeatMap, no guard — component handles its own redirect), `screenings/:id/summary` and `screenings/:id/checkout` (guarded by `bookingGuard`), `confirmation` (guarded by `confirmationGuard`), `**` → `redirectTo: ''`.\n\n   - **`apps/cinescope/src/app/features/movie-list/movie-list.ts` + `.html` + `.scss`** (created): Day picker (Today + 4 weekday buttons + Material datepicker), status-driven movie list (`loading`/`error`/`loaded`), client-side filtering of a single fetched movies+screenings payload by `selectedDate` computed signal, `data-testid`s per spec 9.1.\n\n   - **`apps/cinescope/src/app/features/seat-map/seat-map.ts` + `.html` + `.scss`** (created, with one self-caught bug fix): Full seat-map feature — grid rendering of `ROW_LAYOUTS`, seat/couch state coloring, selection toggling with toast on limit, selected-seats panel, cancel/continue actions. **Bug caught before testing**: an initial `signalFromId` helper function incorrectly tried to derive a `computed()` signal from mutations of a plain JS object (`result.current`), which doesn't trigger Angular change detection since `computed()` only tracks signal reads. Fixed by replacing it with a real `signal<ScreeningData | null>(null)` (`dataSignal`) set via `.set()` inside a proper RxJS subscription in the component constructor using `toObservable(this.id).pipe(switchMap(...), takeUntilDestroyed())`.\n\n   - **`apps/cinescope/src/app/features/summary/summary.ts` + `.html` + `.scss`** (created): Ticket list derived from `buildBookingItems`, `Remove` navigates back to seat map when the booking becomes empty, `Total:` line, Back/Confirm buttons.\n\n   - **`apps/cinescope/src/app/features/checkout/checkout.ts` + `.html` + `.scss`** (created): Custom (non-Reactive-Forms) validation with pure per-field error functions, `touched`/`submitted` signals gating message visibility, `pay()` method performing full validation-then-POST flow with `processing` signal and toasts on invalid/failure, success path calls `bookingService.markPaid(email)` then navigates to `/confirmation`.\n\n   - **`apps/cinescope/src/app/features/confirmation/confirmation.ts` + `.html` + `.scss`** (created): Shows email from booking, `Continue` clears booking and navigates to `/`.\n\n   - **`/tmp/pw-test/test1.js`** (created, scratch test script, not part of the project): Playwright-core driven end-to-end smoke test script covering movie list → (direct nav to `/screenings/1/seats` due to the date mismatch) → seat-map → selection → summary → checkout (invalid then valid submission) → confirmation → back to movie list, with console-error capture and screenshots written to `/tmp/pw-test/*.png`.\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - **pnpm interactive prompt blocking build**: `pnpm nx build cinescope` failed with `ERR_PNPM_ABORTED_REMOVE_MODULES_DIR_NO_TTY` because pnpm wanted to reinstall node_modules interactively. Fixed by running with `CI=true pnpm nx build cinescope` for that one invocation.\n   - **Build failure: `Could not resolve \"@angular/animations/browser\"`**: Caused by `provideAnimationsAsync()` in `app.config.ts`, which requires the `@angular/animations` package that is not an installed dependency (and the user's constraints forbid adding dependencies). Fixed by removing `provideAnimationsAsync()` and its import entirely; subsequent build succeeded (with only a non-blocking bundle-size budget warning: 685.33 kB vs. the 500 kB *warning* threshold, well under the 1 MB *error* threshold, so the build still \"succeeds\").\n   - **Broken signal derivation in `seat-map.ts`**: Caught and fixed myself (see Files section above) before ever building/testing — replaced a non-reactive object-mutation hack with a proper `signal()` + RxJS subscription pattern used consistently across seat-map/summary/checkout.\n   - **Unused `HttpParams` import in `api.service.ts`**: Removed since all screenings are fetched in bulk and filtered client-side, so the query-param-based endpoint variants weren't used in `ApiService`'s final implementation.\n   - **Background task / log-buffering issues during manual browser testing**: A `node test1.js 2>&1 | tail -150`-style invocation under `run_in_background` produced an empty output file until the pipe closed, misleading me into thinking nothing had run. Fixed by redirecting directly to a log file (`> /tmp/pw-test/out.log 2>&1; echo DONE >> /tmp/pw-test/out.log`) and using `Monitor` with an until-loop polling for the `DONE` marker instead of piping through `tail`.\n   - **Movie list showing 0 movie cards during testing**: Not a bug — caused by the sandbox's real \"today\" (2026-10-15) being outside db.json's screening date range (2026-09-15 to 2026-09-21), which the spec explicitly says is expected behavior and must not be \"fixed\" by altering `db.json` or date logic. Adapted the test script to navigate directly to `/screenings/1/seats` by URL instead of clicking through from the movie list.\n   - **Test script appeared to hang after \"toast after invalid submit\" log line**: Not yet confirmed as a real bug at the time of this summary — hypothesized to be either (a) genuine Playwright auto-wait behavior (each `.textContent()` call on a locator retries for up to the default 30s timeout, and with 5 sequential error-locator calls this could add up to significant wall-clock time even if all elements are actually present and correct), or (b) a real rendering issue where the touched/submitted state isn't propagating to the template under zoneless change detection. This was still being investigated (via a backgrounded run with a 5-minute Monitor) when the summary-only interruption arrived — **unresolved at time of this summary**.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - Solved: Correct Nx/Angular/Material build configuration without needing `@angular/animations`.\n   - Solved: Clean separation of static auditorium geometry (track-based `ROW_LAYOUTS`, computed once) from dynamic per-cell state (computed from `occupied`/`selected` Sets derived from signals), verified correct via live smoke test (296 seats, 12 couches, 30 aisles, correct accessible-seat/couch/occupied-seat states matching db.json's screening 1 occupiedSeats).\n   - Solved: `sessionStorage`-backed booking persisted via a signal + `effect()`, with atomic couch pair toggling and a 10-seat cap, verified live (selecting 2 seats + 1 couch → \"Selected seats: 4\").\n   - Solved: Summary/pricing math verified live (25.00 + 25.00 + 89.00 = 139.00 PLN, matching spec's price tiers).\n   - Solved: Checkout pay-button label and \"form contains errors\" toast verified live for the invalid/empty-form case.\n   - **Ongoing/unresolved at interruption**: whether checkout per-field validation messages (`first-name-error`, `last-name-error`, `email-error`, `confirm-email-error`, `terms-error`) actually render correctly after an invalid submit attempt — the smoke-test script's log output stalled right after confirming the toast appeared, before confirming the individual field error messages. A background Monitor (task id `byj93w3bv`, watching `/tmp/pw-test/out.log` for a `DONE` marker, 5-minute timeout) was armed to catch the script's completion, but no result had arrived before this summary was requested.\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - The initial (and only substantive) user instruction: \"Build the cinema seat-booking web application described in spec/README.md, as the Angular application already set up in this Nx workspace (Nx project `cinescope` in apps/cinescope); its stack is described in spec/stack.md. The work is split into tickets in spec/tickets/; implement them in order. spec/README.md is the complete specification: do not ask any questions, and where it is silent choose the simplest option that satisfies it. Finish only when every ticket is done and `pnpm nx build cinescope` succeeds.\"\n   - The final message (system-level, not a genuine user chat message, but delivered as the most recent turn) was a forced instruction to produce this summary in plain text only, with no tool calls — this is the message currently being responded to.\n   - No other genuine user-authored chat messages occurred in this session; all intervening content was system-reminders, tool outputs, and automated task-notifications (which per instructions must never be treated as user input, approval, or confirmation).\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - Finish verifying the checkout validation-message rendering (the in-progress smoke test) and confirm no real bug exists (or fix one if found).\n   - Complete remaining acceptance-criteria verification across all tickets, in particular: phone-number validation message, confirm-email mismatch message, terms-checkbox required message, pay button \"Processing…\" state during the in-flight reque